{"relation":"dlktk/discussion","args":{"id":"papij-domaj","title":"V1.2 loop termination guard","subject":"q:monotonic-drift-shrink guard vs max-iter cap + drift==0 fixed point","created_by":"chazu"},"source":"chazu","valid_start":1782086017}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"mafih-sudid","disc":"papij-domaj","kind":"argument","text":"The cap already bounds any future oscillator (it halts regardless); the guard only saves iterations, and YAGNI says build it when that consumer actually appears (revisit-trigger), not speculatively","author":"shipper-bot"},"source":"shipper-bot","valid_start":1782086074}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"madov-sudah","disc":"papij-domaj","kind":"argument","text":"Absence of an oscillating consumer today is not absence tomorrow; a shrink guard is cheap insurance against a future model that does oscillate","author":"maint-bot"},"source":"maint-bot","valid_start":1782086074}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"jamig-zudot","disc":"papij-domaj","kind":"argument","text":"Use a set-identity metric (the drift diff-set itself), not a count: identical successive diff-sets = no progress, with zero false positives — the ambiguity disappears","author":"maint-bot"},"source":"maint-bot","valid_start":1782086062}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"dakud-tonut","disc":"papij-domaj","kind":"argument","text":"A diff-count shrink metric is ambiguous: count can stay flat while the set changes (one diff resolves, one appears), causing false 'stuck' stops that abort legitimate non-monotonic progress","author":"sec-bot"},"source":"sec-bot","valid_start":1782086046}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"dakit-zijig","disc":"papij-domaj","kind":"argument","text":"No worked convergence consumer oscillates: examples 1,3,4 are all set-difference (create/delete/update), so the guard solves a problem no consumer has","author":"historian-bot"},"source":"historian-bot","valid_start":1782086046}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"dakan-fahaf","disc":"papij-domaj","kind":"argument","text":"Cap default is 5 and set-difference converges in 1-2; wasted work is bounded, cheap, and the failure is still reported either way","author":"shipper-bot"},"source":"shipper-bot","valid_start":1782086046}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"dajug-tusib","disc":"papij-domaj","kind":"argument","text":"Without a shrink guard a stuck/oscillating loop burns all N iterations doing useless apply-work before it reports failure","author":"maint-bot"},"source":"maint-bot","valid_start":1782086046}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"sugol-pajib","disc":"papij-domaj","kind":"position","text":"Cap + drift==0 AND a monotonic-drift-shrink guard that stops early when drift stops shrinking","author":"maint-bot"},"source":"maint-bot","valid_start":1782086028}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"sugib-kabig","disc":"papij-domaj","kind":"position","text":"Hard max-iter cap + drift==0 fixed point; no monotonic guard","author":"shipper-bot"},"source":"shipper-bot","valid_start":1782086028}
{"relation":"dlktk/node","args":{"id":"sufum-lifus","disc":"papij-domaj","kind":"issue","text":"What guarantees convergence-loop termination?","author":"shipper-bot"},"source":"shipper-bot","valid_start":1782086028}
